From 786aa9faf2d1f00b53d02f9d1ad776b0a283fd36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): scan computed executable word candidates [daveey]

Parameter defaults and command substitution output could form the executable
while the guard inspected only literal executable names and substitution bodies.
Historical literal-variable support intentionally adds execution candidates; no
historical exclusion of computed executable names was found.

Keep expansion spans opaque while establishing structural executable positions.
Add literal default and simple printer-output readings without executing text;
retain set-variable sinks for later sourced bindings. Refuse unresolved actual
computed executable words after ordinary lifecycle/cap traversal. Preserve
arithmetic/data provenance and revoke printer assumptions for visible functions
and alias uncertainty, including later sourced definitions.

One intentional compatibility change: executing output of a lifecycle-clean
Python producer is no longer proved safe merely by scanning the producer; the
existing backtick clean-script test now expects an unresolved-output refusal.
Ordinary data arguments and literal clean default/output twins remain allowed.

Proof: baseline 11 failures/10 passing clean controls; real Bash marker stubs
execute all RUN cases without touching services. Expanded 34 focused cases;
all 67 tests/cron lifecycle consumers pass (10506 tests). scripts/check --base
origin/main passes. PR2925 untouched. PR3358 handles computed shell inputs at a
separate traversal seam; this change covers executable words/parameter defaults.
